                <pb facs="0818" n="690" sameAs="frus:frus1928v01/pg690"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.3415/267a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Bolivia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Kaufman</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-12-13T19:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 13,
                                1928—7 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>34. The International Conference of American States on Conciliation and
                    Arbitration will hold a plenary session tomorrow morning at 11 o’clock to
                    receive the report of the Special Committee appointed by the Conference to
                    consider the situation which has developed between Bolivia and Paraguay. I
                    understand that this report will recommend <pb facs="0819" n="691"
                        xml:id="pg691"/> to the Conference that the Conference tender its good
                    offices to the Governments of Bolivia and Paraguay for the purpose of aiding
                    them in providing such conciliatory measures as may be found appropriate to the
                    end that conflict may be avoided and peace maintained. Please go at once to the
                    President of the Republic and give him the above information and tell him that I
                    earnestly urge that nothing shall be done to make abortive the tender of good
                    offices by the Conference which I hope will be found welcome.</p>
                <p>Like message being sent to Paraguay.<anchor n="65" xml:id="d469-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kaufman</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
